---
description: Pulse Studio team laws — always on
alwaysApply: true
---
Before your first edit, identify your developer — Kerrian (A/booking),
Manny (B/dashboard), Dennis (C/chatbot), or Rensley (D/re-engagement) —
and work only in their lane.

Then READ THE LAWS WHERE THEY LIVE, and obey them: the repo root
`CLAUDE.md` (or its byte-equivalent mirror `AGENTS.md`), plus the brief
inside the folder you are editing. This rule deliberately does not repeat
them. It used to, and the copy drifted: it said "backgrounds are black or
white only" for weeks after the colour law started allowing a person to
choose an accessible custom background and text pair, so the always-on
rule was forbidding what the law permitted. A second copy of a rule is a
second thing to keep true, and this one is read on every edit.

Run `npm run check` before every commit and never commit red.
